sanctioned: this program uses Db.open + Db.withTransaction + Db.exec (SqlValue params) + Db.unsafeFindWhere (parameterised WHERE with List String args bound via ? placeholders) — the Go backend and ipê share the Sky stdlib surface but the Go reference emits Go+SQLite binaries while ipê emits Rust+sqlx; the SQLite in-memory behaviour and row-type representation differ enough that a shared Main.sky cannot run on both backends. ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. The parameterised-args channel is exercised here to prove injection-safe operation on the sole sanctioned raw-SQL path.
